The bug was an off-by-one error in `src/parse.py:4`. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element of the split array) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to incorrectly return `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an `IndexError` since there's no second element

I fixed it by changing `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and all tests now pass.
